SaaS Foundation wraps a number of third-party open-source engines so that
business systems consume them only through the foundation SDK. Each engine
is distributed under its own license and remains the property of its owners.
Notable wrapped components include:

  - Keycloak (identity / OIDC / OAuth2 / SAML)
  - Open Policy Agent (authorization / ABAC)
  - PostgreSQL, PgBouncer, Redis
  - ClickHouse (audit event store)
  - OpenSearch (search)
  - HashiCorp Vault (key management / crypto)
  - LiteLLM (LLM routing backend behind the LLM gateway)
  - MinIO / S3-compatible object storage
  - Unleash (feature flags)
  - OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, Jaeger (observability)

No inference engine is bundled; the LLM gateway forwards to external or
customer-provided model endpoints.
